## Hypotheses

Each hypothesis is stated as the alternative. Its null is that quantum and seeded pseudo-random sampling do not differ on the outcome in that comparison. There is one hypothesis per confirmatory outcome and per (model, sampling) comparison; models and sampling presets are never pooled. The significance level is α = {{ levels.alpha | md }} across all of them together.

Every other endpoint of the selected evals is exploratory. Where the harness computes it, it is reported with an effect size and an interval; an endpoint the harness does not compute is reported as unavailable. An exploratory endpoint is not corrected for multiple testing and decides nothing.
