## Decision rules

A script resolves each hypothesis to exactly one verdict under decision matrix version {{ design.matrix_version }}. The rows are tried in order and the first whose condition holds decides. Nothing in this section is chosen after the data exist.

| # | Condition | Verdict | Reason recorded | Result sentence |
|---|---|---|---|---|
{% for rule in decision_matrix -%}
| {{ rule.number }} | {{ rule.condition | md }} | {{ rule.verdict | md }} | {{ 'the first that applies of ' if rule.reasons | length > 1 else '' }}{{ (rule.reasons | join(', ') or 'none') | md }} | {{ rule.wording | md }} |
{% endfor %}
Terms used in the conditions:

- **alpha** is {{ levels.alpha | md }}, the significance level of the study.
- **pD** is the p-value of the hypothesis's difference test after Holm–Bonferroni correction over every confirmatory hypothesis ({{ design.families.difference }} in this study). A hypothesis whose comparison could not be computed keeps its place in the family at p = 1.
- **pE** is the p-value of the equivalence test against the registered margin, after Holm–Bonferroni correction over every hypothesis that has a margin ({{ design.families.equivalence }} in this study).
- **Planned pairs analysed** is, for a paired test, the complete pairs divided by the planned pairs. For a test on pooled tokens it is the generations present in the arm that has the fewest, divided by the generations planned per arm. A generation is present for the MMD test when its tokens were recorded, and for the KS test when they were recorded with the cumulative probabilities that test is computed from. The threshold is {{ levels.min_completeness | md }}.
- **The claim includes equivalence** {{ 'in this study.' if design.claim == 'difference_or_equivalence' else 'in no hypothesis of this study, which registers a claim of difference only.' }}
- **The seed-vs-seed control** and **the positive control** are defined under Controls below.

